{
  "about": "Expected behavior is what the Standard's text says. 'control' cases must behave as expected; a mismatch fails CI. 'known-defect' cases document where reference release 5.1.2 differs from the text; while the defect's status is 'open', a mismatch is reported, not failed. When a fix is merged, set the defect's status to 'fixed' in the same pull request so its cases are enforced from then on.",
  "defects": {
    "KD-01": {
      "summary": "The schemas' own $id addresses (/schemas/v5.0/...) do not match where the files are served (/standard/v5.0/...), so the decision record's link to the attestation schema cannot be resolved by a standard validator.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    "KD-02": {
      "summary": "A record that omits record_type is treated as a redaction event. The text says an omitted record_type means decision.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-03": {
      "summary": "Redaction fields: the allowed values of redaction_basis and the sub-fields of redaction_authority and operational_store_deletion_attestation differ from the Section 6.2.3 table, so a redaction record written as the text describes is rejected.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-04": {
      "summary": "Section 6.2.2 requires disclosure_metadata_pointer from drafted for mode-1-with-embedded-mode-2-summary records within the §4.6 requirement; the schema does not enforce it.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-05": {
      "summary": "The text requires altitude from the drafted state; the schema never requires it, and a missing altitude surfaces as an unrelated consent_posture error.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-06": {
      "summary": "Disclosure block: the text requires 5 fields, the schema 7; the text's jurisdiction and content-type spellings (including other:<...>) are rejected.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-07": {
      "summary": "For mode-2 records the schema requires disclosure_metadata_pointer already at dispatched; the text requires it from drafted, and only for records within the §4.6 requirement.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-08": {
      "summary": "Sections 4.6.2 and 2.2.12 accept a declaring authority that names only the person or only the organization; the disclosure schema's declaring_authority object requires a person's full_name, role_title and capacity and the employer, so a value that names only one of them is rejected.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-09": {
      "summary": "The reference Charter state machine requires a peer_reviewer_pool of at least 3 named individuals before fields-completed, and the Charter schema rejects any pool smaller than 3; the text (Sections 3.2 and 3.3) requires neither. The state-machine rule is prose and is not machine-checked here; the case covers the schema's pool size.",
      "status": "open"
    },
    "KD-10": {
      "summary": "For outputs a Charter places outside the disclosure requirement (§4.6.1), the text requires no disclosure_metadata_pointer; the schema requires it on every mode-2 record, and cannot see the Charter's declaration.",
      "status": "fixed"
    },
    "KD-11": {
      "summary": "Section 3.1 recommends (SHOULD) the named_employment_counsel_of_record Charter field; the Charter schema allows no properties beyond its list and rejects a Charter that carries it.",
      "status": "open"
    }
  },
